 All product endpoints are JSON endpoints under `/api/v1`. Requests other than account creation select a business with `X-Helpdesk-Account`. Authenticated requests use `Authorization: Bearer TOKEN`.
 
-Customers register at `POST /api/v1/registrations`, then use the standard verification and session endpoints. Authenticated customers use `/api/v1/requests` and its nested `/comments` route; staff use `/api/v1/tickets`. Replies, status changes, and active-staff assignments are submitted with `PATCH`. Private staff comments are excluded from customer comment responses and do not touch the customer request timestamp. Lists accept `page` and `per_page` and include pagination metadata with the records.
+Customers register at `POST /api/v1/registrations`, then use the standard verification and session endpoints. Authenticated customers use `/api/v1/requests` and its nested `/comments` route; staff use `/api/v1/tickets`. Replies, status changes, and active-staff assignments are submitted with `PATCH`. Private staff comments are excluded from customer comment responses and do not touch the customer request timestamp.
+
+All collection endpoints support cursor pagination with `page[size]`, `page[after]`, and `page[before]`. Responses retain the collection records and include `meta` (`has_more`, `after_cursor`, `before_cursor`) and absolute `links` (`next`, `prev`). Cursors are opaque, preserve the active filters and ordering, and keep an in-progress browse stable as records are added. The legacy offset API remains available through `page` and `per_page` (or `page[number]` and `page[size]`) and retains its count and page metadata.
 
 Staff can set each ticket's `priority` to `normal` (the default) or `high`. Staff ticket responses include priority, while customer request responses do not. Staff can combine `status`, `assignee_id`, `group_id`, `requester_id`, `priority`, and `q` filters on `/api/v1/tickets`; `assignee_id=unassigned` selects tickets without an assignee. `q` is a case-insensitive literal search of subjects and public comments. Customer request lists support only the `status` filter.
 
